+## Worker ledger
+
+Pass `--task <TASK-ID>` on every launch. The value is recorded verbatim and is
+never inferred when the flag is absent. An installed launch always writes the
+target's fixed `.brichan/ledger/workers.jsonl`; there is no ledger-location
+option, and `--ledger-file` is rejected as an unrecognized argument (exit `2`)
+before any Herdr call.
+
+A successful launch appends exactly one `launched` record and prints
+`ledger: launch_id=<uuid>` on stderr; stdout stays the verbatim
+`agent_started` envelope. Record that `launch_id` in project memory with the
+worker's name and pane ID. A launch that rolls back appends nothing, and
+`--dry-run` and `--json` write nothing. A ledger failure after a start prints
+`warning: worker started but ledger write failed: <reason>` and changes
+nothing else: the exit code stays `0` and the worker stays up. A named-route
+launch always resolves the fixed ledger; only a legacy launch with an explicit
+command after `--` whose `--cwd` is not inside an initialized target prints
+`ledger: no ledger location for this launch; not recorded` and proceeds.
+
+Record the worker's end only from evidence, never from scheduling state:
+
+```text
+brichan-herdr-worker-ledger finish \
+  --project <absolute-target-project> \
+  --worker <brichan-name> \
+  --launch-id <uuid> \
+  --evidence <repo-relative-path> [--evidence <citation> ...] \
+  [--task <TASK-ID>] [--pane <pane-id>]
+```
+
+`--project` names the target's Git root, whose `.brichan/ledger/workers.jsonl`
+receives the record; without it, the Git root found upward from the current
+directory is used. A `finished` record is a coordinator attestation, not proof:
+the command cannot verify completion. It refuses a `--launch-id` that matches
+no `launched` record, a `--launch-id` that already has a `finished` record, a
+worker name without the `brichan-` prefix, an empty or whitespace-only
+`--evidence` item, and a target that is not a Git root or has no regular
+`.brichan/manifest.json`, each with exit `1` and nothing written. Each launch
+takes at most one attestation; when two `finish` runs overlap, consumers take
+the first `finished` record for that `launch_id` in file order as the winning
+one.
+Absence of a `finished` record means "unknown", never "still running" or
+"failed".
+
+| Exit | Meaning |
+|---:|---|
+| `0` | Attestation recorded |
+| `1` | Refused or failed (no ledger, unmatched or already-finished `launch_id`, write failure) |
+| `2` | Invalid invocation, including a missing required flag or `--ledger-file` |
+
